  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Interacting with other users on VRChat is a thrill, and with the new Avatar Dynamics, it has become even better! \nSeeing the new IK system where the arms wrap neatly around the avatar's body made me think it would be great to be able to interact with other players in a more \"realistic\" way, i.e, not being able to go through someone's avatar, being able to hug your friends without having this awkward moment of attempting to place your hands around them properly, as they tend to traverse their polygonal-selves. Instead, your avatar would neatly surround your friend's body, just like in real life. You could Headpat without Brainpatting, give a kiss on the cheek without seeing their globulous eyes. \nOf course, just like interactions with Avatar Dynamics, one should be able to opt in and out of the system at a button's press, and decide who this system would work with and who it wouldn't, similar to Avatar Dynamics once again.",
